{"title":"2011 AIME II Problems/Problem 15","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Graphing)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Graphing)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(Solution_1)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (Solution 1)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/8/d486d57c1d244aeef20ddf5786265375269bfa7f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(x) = x^2 - 3x - 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"153\" height=\"19\" />. A real number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is chosen at random from the interval <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/1/011a2ff8ed38676d2e84d6b06991d649354637fc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5 \\le x \\le 15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"85\" height=\"15\" />. The probability that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/b/5cbf91ce9c52f5dae245e09f3c0657d27c1722c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left\\lfloor\\sqrt{P(x)}\\right\\rfloor = \\sqrt{P(\\left\\lfloor x \\right\\rfloor)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"176\" height=\"45\" /> is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/e/17e7a83eb9a324579e4291f634614954b06b7056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\sqrt{a} + \\sqrt{b} + \\sqrt{c} - d}{e}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"149\" height=\"41\" /> , where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/a/a3a59bb1293ee3f6dec19de4019a7178874219ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$e$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> are positive integers. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/1/a519928302764a4b4d150f04acef573cf4ed10ed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a + b + c + d + e$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"134\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Table of values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/f/6efaaf74e576202fad965134bc49c6a34aac4c30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" />:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/3/4b311417d1340823619cd840bd94fb9c0442b99f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} P(5) &amp;= 1 \\\\ P(6) &amp;= 9 \\\\ P(7) &amp;= 19 \\\\ P(8) &amp;= 31 \\\\ P(9) &amp;= 45 \\\\ P(10) &amp;= 61 \\\\ P(11) &amp;= 79 \\\\ P(12) &amp;= 99 \\\\ P(13) &amp;= 121 \\\\ P(14) &amp;= 145 \\\\ P(15) &amp;= 171 \\\\ \\end{align*}\" width=\"96\" height=\"267\" />\n</p><p>In order for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/1/b2139e8523888601a15943aabdca0a9accc19bd3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lfloor \\sqrt{P(x)} \\rfloor = \\sqrt{P(\\lfloor x \\rfloor)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"169\" height=\"32\" /> to hold, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/1/401556b082213508260d8521472ed359d0c6cc01.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{P(\\lfloor x \\rfloor)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"73\" height=\"32\" /> must be an integer and hence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/1/5314f2686d95cb2dd201a27e5ddac08d4c527a85.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(\\lfloor x \\rfloor)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"57\" height=\"20\" /> must be a perfect square. This limits <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/6/d16a33db31b81eef5568823dbee218e1dcefeda8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5 \\le x &lt; 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"76\" height=\"15\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/c/4fc403c366c4eab4b509849df452fcfb38f6d5cd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6 \\le x &lt; 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"77\" height=\"15\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/e/88e1cd25484bd91fe923ab56fea7a1e91d4522a8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13 \\le x &lt; 14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"95\" height=\"15\" /> since, from the table above, those are the only values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> for which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/1/5314f2686d95cb2dd201a27e5ddac08d4c527a85.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(\\lfloor x \\rfloor)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"57\" height=\"20\" /> is a perfect square. However, in order for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/3/0d35ca11d42a271a70e8d4e26758cf46664e8b92.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{P(x)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"57\" height=\"32\" /> to be rounded down to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/1/5314f2686d95cb2dd201a27e5ddac08d4c527a85.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(\\lfloor x \\rfloor)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"57\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/f/6efaaf74e576202fad965134bc49c6a34aac4c30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" /> must be less than the next perfect square after <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/1/5314f2686d95cb2dd201a27e5ddac08d4c527a85.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(\\lfloor x \\rfloor)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"57\" height=\"20\" /> (for the said intervals). Now, we consider the three cases:\n</p><p><br />\nCase <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/6/d16a33db31b81eef5568823dbee218e1dcefeda8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5 \\le x &lt; 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"76\" height=\"15\" />:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/f/6efaaf74e576202fad965134bc49c6a34aac4c30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" /> must be less than the first perfect square after <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <i>i.e.</i>:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/b/5cb267a14e634206cc36f096b83a66c6401710c3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\le P(x) &lt; 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"105\" height=\"18\" /> (because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/2/502dba5ec85a70189b6e3662e80a6e7f935227d8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lfloor \\sqrt{P(x)} \\rfloor = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"105\" height=\"32\" /> implies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/9/d7932bdf2dcc664753346c460c8abf7add854e0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\le \\sqrt{P(x)} &lt; 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"122\" height=\"32\" />)\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/f/6efaaf74e576202fad965134bc49c6a34aac4c30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" /> is increasing for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/1/1014b7700db9eb58f5543dda52308d1dd1632ecf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x \\ge 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"46\" height=\"16\" />, we just need to find the value <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/e/d0e15703b4f9cc33ff0c4642663d183b5c4557c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$v \\ge 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/1/111096d368568bb6ab402215a7c874bbd1510eaa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(v) = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"71\" height=\"18\" />, which will give us the working range <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/c/68c5ab012cce6983bced65415bc9732e0611c310.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5 \\le x &lt; v$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"77\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/1/6a1bca40d32144b4b906c6a211a0af4d52c7e90c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} v^2 - 3v - 9 &amp;= 4 \\\\ v &amp;= \\frac{3 + \\sqrt{61}}{2} \\end{align*}\" width=\"179\" height=\"69\" />\n</p><p>So in this case, the only values that will work are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/e/d2e60167e4d72b3c143a7ac5724abbbf7ee531b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5 \\le x &lt; \\frac{3 + \\sqrt{61}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"135\" height=\"41\" />.\n</p><p>Case <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/c/4fc403c366c4eab4b509849df452fcfb38f6d5cd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6 \\le x &lt; 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"77\" height=\"15\" />:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/f/6efaaf74e576202fad965134bc49c6a34aac4c30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" /> must be less than the first perfect square after <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/5/9a5b4928c8fe50ce3c2428da3bee3505e891b788.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/a/f8adefb5f45701cbcafb0b683efa68d35020a2f2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} v^2 - 3v - 9 &amp;= 16 \\\\ v &amp;= \\frac{3 + \\sqrt{109}}{2} \\end{align*}\" width=\"188\" height=\"69\" />\n</p><p>So in this case, the only values that will work are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/4/c1469d459b231016be83cb8d6d0a2ba025bdaf4a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6 \\le x &lt; \\frac{3 + \\sqrt{109}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"144\" height=\"41\" />.\n</p><p>Case <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/e/88e1cd25484bd91fe923ab56fea7a1e91d4522a8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13 \\le x &lt; 14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"95\" height=\"15\" />:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/f/6efaaf74e576202fad965134bc49c6a34aac4c30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" /> must be less than the first perfect square after <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/a/76ad7692f5d86be790209a56a68c2a3488235054.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$121$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" />, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/f/50ff9540650f0f95f80da2f6692fc8ee413e2eb3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$144$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"27\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/7/f67342a9d0cdc9d488f4e0b544d308c13b1a07cf.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} v^2 - 3v - 9 &amp;= 144 \\\\ v &amp;= \\frac{3 + \\sqrt{621}}{2} \\end{align*}\" width=\"188\" height=\"69\" />\n</p><p>So in this case, the only values that will work are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/8/468f2a2767741ff46906a58feeeeb404fa792357.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13 \\le x &lt; \\frac{3 + \\sqrt{621}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"153\" height=\"41\" />.\n</p><p>Now, we find the length of the working intervals and divide it by the length of the total interval, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/b/f0b686cd92ee8f20bb7c98f01364750863b52ffa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15 - 5 = 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"91\" height=\"13\" />:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/e/74ed7caf45857a8e3335ef4bcabdad4f60f3c030.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} \\frac{\\left( \\frac{3 + \\sqrt{61}}{2} - 5 \\right) + \\left( \\frac{3 + \\sqrt{109}}{2} - 6 \\right) + \\left( \\frac{3 + \\sqrt{621}}{2} - 13 \\right)}{10} \\\\ &amp;= \\frac{\\sqrt{61} + \\sqrt{109} + \\sqrt{621} - 39}{20} \\end{align*}\" width=\"591\" height=\"100\" />\n</p><p>Thus, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/3/873be25c17089210848f5f75f895af7ed698af82.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$61 + 109 + 621 + 39 + 20 = \\fbox{850}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"258\" height=\"22\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Make the substitution <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9e7dbfff55c9f686eadbcfb17f8f9e086ea5d3f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=2x-3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"84\" height=\"16\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/a/aba4eae0e78e347a9e1a6d8499eab6c81357e40f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(x)=\\frac{y^2-45}{4}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"131\" height=\"41\" /> We're looking for solutions to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/7/787fed2bc80f1555ce140ff37036f1dbc7abd926.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\bigg\\lfloor{\\sqrt{\\frac{y^2-45}{4}}\\bigg\\rfloor}=\\sqrt{\\frac{\\lfloor{y\\rfloor}^2-45}{4}}\\]\" width=\"216\" height=\"54\" />with the new bounds <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/7/5b7098415b6f199981300df83aea7089e4e65221.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y\\in{[7,27]}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"75\" height=\"18\" />. Since the left side is an integer, it must be that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/9/59991f923139161ae75379d0d14266352276c29b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\lfloor{y\\rfloor}^2-45}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"76\" height=\"42\" /> is a perfect square. For simplicity, write <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/4/1040e0ebbc4b020d1218acbd960fd95557d3941e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lfloor{y\\rfloor}=a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"61\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/c/f0c5b08c728e311f7ba7f38d40c9b399d818b768.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a^2-45=4b^2\\implies{(a-2b)(a+2b)=45}.\\]\" width=\"327\" height=\"19\" />Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/d/27d726a1d298d560c173387e8644bd229d92f887.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a-2b&lt;a+2b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"122\" height=\"14\" />, it must be that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/b/f3b9be7f18a024112ecb46670379ced7fbc8964b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a-2b,a+2b)=(1,45),(3,15),(5,9)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"298\" height=\"18\" />, which gives solutions <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/f/09f9a03effc00d96a102bb294aaf8398a3b2fc8c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(23,11),(9,3),(7,1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"154\" height=\"18\" />, respectively. But this gives us three cases to check:\n</p><p>Case 1: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/d/37d54467f04270830c1994d52cf2a142977121ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\bigg\\lfloor{\\sqrt{\\frac{y^2-45}{4}}\\bigg\\rfloor}=11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"141\" height=\"46\" />.\n</p><p>In this case, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/0/b8098d7e2a19073870b4dfa4adaa9a4e95f05142.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[11\\leq{\\sqrt{\\frac{y^2-45}{4}}}&lt;12\\implies{y\\in{[23,\\sqrt{621})}}.\\]\" width=\"328\" height=\"43\" />\nCase 2: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/6/f46d65fe193f26428f3c1234ff97f4f8f7333280.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\bigg\\lfloor{\\sqrt{\\frac{y^2-45}{4}}\\bigg\\rfloor}=3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"132\" height=\"46\" />.\n</p><p>In this case, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/3/043ca2b6d9aa65a3a7cfbe5545c233bd15e6636f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[3\\leq{\\sqrt{\\frac{y^2-45}{4}}}&lt;4\\implies{y\\in{[9,\\sqrt{109})}}.\\]\" width=\"302\" height=\"43\" />\nCase 3: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/0/560a663c3a8b866da738e2994ec657ad79af80c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\bigg\\lfloor{\\sqrt{\\frac{y^2-45}{4}}\\bigg\\rfloor}=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"132\" height=\"46\" />\n</p><p>In this case, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/d/66d4cc2b96b32124aead3546596bd962df822c4f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[1\\leq{\\sqrt{\\frac{y^2-45}{4}}}&lt;2\\implies{y\\in{[7,\\sqrt{61})}}.\\]\" width=\"292\" height=\"43\" />\nTo finish, the total length of the interval from which we choose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/e/4fe442cd39f0faba5002273bfc64a33459b3b5a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$27-7=20$\" width=\"91\" height=\"12\" />. The total length of the success intervals is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/d/e3d788459ffab7d54b9e1cba3b30d8f744b89063.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(\\sqrt{61}-7)+(\\sqrt{109}-9)+(\\sqrt{621}-23)=\\sqrt{61}+\\sqrt{109}+\\sqrt{621}-39,\\]\" width=\"477\" height=\"21\" />which means the probability is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/a/75a6d5fb1877ef9308251f21a1c62f888b36b569.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{\\sqrt{61}+\\sqrt{109}+\\sqrt{621}-39}{20}.\\]\" width=\"208\" height=\"41\" />The requested sum is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/1/93171c7d4fcdd25e8c3690afeb801531b871947a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{850}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Graphing.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Graphing)\">Solution 3 (Graphing)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Graphing)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>It's definitely possible to conceptualize this problem visually, if that's your thing, since it is a geometric probability problem. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/c/eecbf5c4f82853886426116a22162dc76d7db923.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A = \\left\\lfloor\\sqrt{P(x)}\\right\\rfloor$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"117\" height=\"45\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/7/227328ddc3bee6fc60e40f4c19fd30754c3bb784.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B = \\sqrt{P(\\left\\lfloor x \\right\\rfloor)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"113\" height=\"35\" />. The graph of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> will look like this, with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> having only integral y-values and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> having only integral x-values:\n</p><p><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:2011_AIME_II_Problem_15_Graph_1.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/a/aa/2011_AIME_II_Problem_15_Graph_1.png/400px-2011_AIME_II_Problem_15_Graph_1.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"400\" height=\"255\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/a/aa/2011_AIME_II_Problem_15_Graph_1.png/600px-2011_AIME_II_Problem_15_Graph_1.png 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/a/aa/2011_AIME_II_Problem_15_Graph_1.png/800px-2011_AIME_II_Problem_15_Graph_1.png 2x\" /></a></span>\n</p><p>As both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> consist of a bunch of line segments, the probability that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/7/1f78f9368d4ac4bebfb371b8a27e702460e7cde9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A = B$\" width=\"52\" height=\"13\" /> is the \"length\" of the overlap between the segments of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> divided by the total length of the segments of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />. \n</p><p>Looking at the graph, we see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> will overlap only when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> is an integer. Specifically, each region of overlap will begin when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/8/e087bcb10d9f9432a70902e207bb35007843c411.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{P(x)}\\ = k,  5 \\le x \\le 15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"190\" height=\"32\" /> has solutions for integral <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> in the range of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />, which consists of the integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/6/1a67a117bdedc1ccda737f78c71569180c7d462c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1-13$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"49\" height=\"13\" />, and end when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> jumps up to its next y-value.\n</p><p>Using the quadratic formula, we see that the start point of each of these overlapping segments will be the integral values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/a/63a5f4d698a249ef1a156c9df7c5762bed87e205.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3 + \\sqrt{45 + 4k^2}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"115\" height=\"40\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> in the specified range, meaning <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/8/fc8b5c9922d65272d4646cc22cb9c6218be99666.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$45 + 4k^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"65\" height=\"16\" /> must be a perfect square. Plugging in all the possible values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/5/915672486d987a1a34162e48dc5861324ee7faf0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k = 1, 3, 11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"85\" height=\"16\" />, corresponding to start points of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/4/634be81c635ed7ed96a87acee3e892d06115edaa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 5, 6, 13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"86\" height=\"16\" />. As already stated, the endpoints will occur when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> jumps up to the next integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/5/f05f085f774fc8ab50676b778b86a1f1d1114fc8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" /> at each of these segments, at which point the x-value will be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/1/9111e87e4ca673213c6c097d69b4aa8979747324.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3 + \\sqrt{45 + 4(k+1)^2}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"164\" height=\"41\" />. On the graph, the overlapping segments of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> would be represented by the highlighted green segments below:\n</p><p><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:2011_AIME_II_Problem_15_Graph_2.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/8/8f/2011_AIME_II_Problem_15_Graph_2.png/400px-2011_AIME_II_Problem_15_Graph_2.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"400\" height=\"302\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/8/8f/2011_AIME_II_Problem_15_Graph_2.png/600px-2011_AIME_II_Problem_15_Graph_2.png 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/8/8f/2011_AIME_II_Problem_15_Graph_2.png/800px-2011_AIME_II_Problem_15_Graph_2.png 2x\" /></a></span>\n</p><p><br />\nTaking the difference between this second x-value and the start point for each of our start points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/4/634be81c635ed7ed96a87acee3e892d06115edaa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 5, 6, 13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"86\" height=\"16\" /> and summing them will give us the total length of these green segments. We can then divide this value by ten (the total length of the segments of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />) to give us the probability of overlap between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Doing so gives us:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/2/d42c055c0431827ceabe47d87b991d77fc100f17.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\left( \\frac{3 + \\sqrt{61}}{2} - 5 \\right) + \\left( \\frac{3 + \\sqrt{109}}{2} - 6 \\right) + \\left( \\frac{3 + \\sqrt{621}}{2} - 13 \\right)}{10} = \\frac{\\sqrt{61} + \\sqrt{109} + \\sqrt{621} - 39}{20}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"593\" height=\"52\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/d/66d78443e682a3d112b739c8f886163cc3cfbe64.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\implies{61 + 109 + 621 + 39 + 20 = \\fbox{850}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"303\" height=\"22\" />.\n</p><p>~ anellipticcurveoverq\n</p><p>~ johnxyz1 (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/e/9ee8610379d2a6e33c4b2d36e50bb75025ad1fa3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text\\LaTeX \\mathit{fixes}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"80\" height=\"18\" />)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Note that all the \"bounds\" have to be less than the number+1, otherwise it wouldn't fit the answer format. Therefore, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/c/44cb3b31176dfb6364db087b4b847549a7c26040.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3*3+\\sqrt{9+4(4+9)}-10+\\sqrt{9+4(16+9)}-12+\\sqrt{9+4(144+9)}}{20} \\implies \\boxed{850}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"640\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p>~Lcz\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://youtu.be/HFW4ekFrxEg?si=Ji9OXTdR8zcPlkac\">2011 AIME I #15</a>\n</p><p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://mathproblemsolvingskills.wordpress.com/\">MathProblemSolvingSkills.com</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_.28Solution_1.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_(Solution_1)\">Video Solution (Solution 1)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution (Solution 1)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/insYfMGpmq4\">https://youtu.be/insYfMGpmq4</a> - Continuum Math\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AIME_II\" title=\"2011 AIME II\">2011 AIME II</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AIME_II_Problems\" title=\"2011 AIME II Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AIME_II_Answer_Key\" title=\"2011 AIME II Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=2011\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2011 AIME II Problems/Problem 14\">Problem 14</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b>Last Problem</b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2011 AIME II Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2011 AIME II Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2011 AIME II Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2011 AIME II Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2011 AIME II Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2011 AIME II Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2011 AIME II Problems/Proble